W3ESXi
Legacy WHMCS integration for VMware ESXi
===============================================================================

PROJECT RETIRED — END OF LIFE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Status:                   RETIRED
Development and releases: DISCONTINUED
Security updates:         NOT PROVIDED
Compatibility updates:    NOT PROVIDED
Support:                  NOT PROVIDED

W3ESXi is no longer maintained or supported. Do not deploy this software to
new or production environments. The instructions below are preserved only for
historical reference; they are not validated against current software.

Current project notice:
https://github.com/bradjtrammell/w3esxi#readme

HISTORICAL RELEASE INFORMATION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version:       0.8.0
Release date:  February 6, 2022
Original scope: WHMCS 7+ module for provisioning and managing servers on
                multiple VMware ESXi hosts
PHP reference: PHP 7.0+ (historical documentation only)

These historical version references do not establish compatibility with
modern releases of PHP, WHMCS, VMware ESXi, or vSphere.

HISTORICAL INSTALLATION NOTES — NOT FOR NEW DEPLOYMENTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following steps are retained for archival context only.

  1. Download the repository archive to the local computer.
  2. Extract the archive.
  3. Upload the contents of the "WHMCS" folder to the WHMCS installation root.
  4. Copy "_CSS/images" to the active template's images folder.
  5. Add the contents of "clientarea_add_css_to_your_template.txt" to the
     template's main stylesheet.
  6. Enable the add-on in the WHMCS administration panel.
  7. Configure an ESXi host in WHMCS server settings.
  8. Create a product and assign the configured server.

These are historical instructions, not a supported or secure deployment
procedure. The former recommendation to seek installation help on the WHMCS
forums is obsolete.

